<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hipponax</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hipponax of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ephesus">Ephesus</a> was a Greek iambic poet of the sixth century BCE who was expelled from Ephesus by its tyrants and lived at Clazomenae. His abusive, comic verse about beggars, thieves and his enemies, written in a mixed Ionic dialect, used the limping iambic metre (choliambic) that he is credited with inventing. Only fragments of his work survive.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hipponax.jpg" alt="Hipponax" width="320" height="319" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Published by Guillaume Rouille(1518?-1589) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hipponax_of_Ephesus.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
